- op: discuss  # 1a5a
  at: '2026-07-05T19:18:54Z'  # 1a5a
  by: agent  # 1a5a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1a5a
  clock: 6  # 1a5a
  nonce: 1a5a  # 1a5a
  message: "HYPERGUMBO-SPIRIT DERIVATION (6-agent ADR/spec precedent workflow + adversarial audit; full analysis: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/design_analyses/wi-javoh-hypergumbo-spirit-derivation_07052026.json). The adversarial audit REFUTED the curated-allowlist answer (my earlier note) as a partial rationalization: an I/O-relevance allowlist re-opens the un-principled hand-curation the high_risk retirement (WI-tijos) closed — there is NO clean invariant separating curl from git (git does more I/O than most of the list). The deadlock dissolves once CLASSIFICATION and COUNTING are separated (ruling A and its refutation conflated them). RESOLUTION (settles the human-ruling fork by precedent): (1) CLASSIFICATION — every bash external-command launch IS a subprocess crossing (arbitrary code exec; ADR-0016 §1 'all launches risky' completeness invariant + the impl-note ruling A added: bash populates subprocess by emitting unresolved external-command edges, NOT via a data-I/O catalog; ADR-0037 identified-external). Do NOT gate classification by an allowlist. (2) HEADLINE HONESTY is a COUNT question, solved by hypergumbo's established count-vs-disclose machinery (external_potential exclusion; WI-huhit/WI-foduh total_io_edges redefinition; dead-code entrypoint_only_dead disclosure): dedup per (caller, command_name) [kills the 171-identical-git artifact]; and IF deduped launches still swamp the curated stdlib subprocess entries on devops repos, SPLIT the headline — count catalog/stdlib subprocess in total_io_edges, DISCLOSE command-mediated launches in a NEW honestly-labeled 'command_launch' cohort (excluded from total_io_edges, NOT hidden, NOT laundered into external_potential's speculative semantics — a lexed curl is definite, unlike the ~96% unresolved-receiver method noise external_potential quarantines). MECHANISM (Design 1, clean): bash.py implicit-else prestamps meta.io_boundary='subprocess' on an is_resolved=False edge with dst_ref=ExternalRef(bash,cmd,cmd); NO bash.yaml (honors ADR-0016 'not via a catalog' + drift-guard contract); NO io_boundary.py consumer change (rides Path A aggregation 1318-1355). Bundle the erlang.yaml os:cmd re-home (mis-classified under env_read L150). REVISES ruling A's gate (denylist -> no classification gate; flood is a count problem) while KEEPING ruling A's correct parts (subprocess classification, no net/fs catalog). awaits_bakeoff_validation (the command_launch-split question is empirical). Ruling A's premise ('closed builtin denylist = principled stopping point') was verified false by the 5-agent flood measurement (~700-823 chains); a filed decision withdrawn on premise re-verification (ADR-0044 L49 precedent). Moving back to todo_hard — classification settled, direction actionable."  # 1a5a
