- op: discuss  # 9b94
  at: '2026-07-05T20:28:44Z'  # 9b94
  by: agent  # 9b94
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9b94
  clock: 9  # 9b94
  nonce: 9b94  # 9b94
  message: "Implemented per the hypergumbo-spirit derivation (CLASSIFICATION vs COUNTING separation) in PR #438 (merged, commit 15c39d628e). Bash external-program launches (name that is neither an in-tree function, resolver-resolved symbol, nor a shell builtin per the comprehensive SHELL_BUILTINS denylist) now emit a calls edge, is_resolved=False with an ExternalRef dst, deduped per (caller, command), prestamping meta.io_boundary='command_launch' — the first producer-persisted io_boundary, an intentional exception to consumer-time derivation per ADR-0016 impl-note ruling A (no catalog to match; only the shell analyzer distinguishes a launch). Classification is never gated by an I/O-relevance allowlist (that would re-open the hand-curation WI-tijos retired); headline honesty is solved by count-vs-disclose: command_launch is a DISCLOSED-only cohort (new command_launch_edges field, added to _DISCLOSED_ONLY_BOUNDARIES) EXCLUDED from total_io_edges, mirroring external_potential (WI-huhit/WI-foduh, INV-pubom). IO_BOUNDARIES_SCHEMA_VERSION 2.0->2.1. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: (a) live end-to-end repro — 'hypergumbo io-boundaries' on a bash script with curl/git(x2)/rm/echo/cd/local reports command_launch_edges=3 (primitives curl,git,rm — git deduped, builtins excluded), total_io_edges=0 (launches held out of headline), schema_version=2.1; (b) production-path TDD tests: TestCommandLaunchEmission (bash producer) + test_command_launch_disclosed_but_excluded_from_total (aggregation). 100% isolation coverage on cli.py/io_boundary.py/bash.py. The original filed repro (42 bash scripts showing 0 I/O chains) is resolved: external launches are now visible while honestly held out of the verified-I/O count. Erlang os:cmd re-home (mis-homed under env_read) deferred to a separate follow-up (out of scope for this bash-focused PR). awaits_bakeoff_validation: the command_launch-cohort split is an empirical blast-radius change across bash-heavy corpora."  # 9b94
